# ---------------- EnemyTypes.events (Task 16 Part D: typed enemy data) ----------------
# Typed enemy definitions, data-driven. `enemy type "Zombie"` copies a type's stats onto the
# enemy's own variables (my Speed, my SightDistance, my Health, my Weapon, my Hostile,
# my ExplosionDeath, my Type), so an enemy sheet never hard-codes them.
#
# HOW IT LOADS: the file is read when the game loads events (and on hot reload), by name —
# EnemyTypes.events — before any actor's `when me appears` runs, so a type is complete on the
# first tick. Attaching it to a sheet is optional; the `when game starts` block below keeps it
# valid as a normal event file.
#
# UNITS: the built-in defaults are TK4's metres (Zombie speed 2, sight 10). This project's TK
# scenes are authored in centimetres (the player moves 45-200, the camera sits at 600), so the
# table below scales a Zombie to 100 cm/s and 200 cm of sight — otherwise the enemy would be
# blind at 10 cm and never chase. Change a type here, not in code.

when game starts
  set ZombieSpeed to 100
  set ZombieSightDistance to 200
  set ZombieHealth to 50
  set ZombieWeapon to "Claws"
  set ZombieHostile to true
  set ZombieExplosionDeath to false

  set TurretSpeed to 0
  set TurretSightDistance to 15
  set TurretHealth to 100
  set TurretWeapon to "Cannon"
  set TurretHostile to true
  set TurretExplosionDeath to true
